WHATNOW

What tam-hide is doing now and what comes next. Read this first; revise it
at the end of every session (work/README-work).

Updated: 2026-11-22, with W5

STATE

  Version 0.0.0 on dev. No authentication or usable locker is implemented
  yet. The minimal C11 seat-controller prototype (src/tam-hided.c,
  src/tam-hidectl.c, src/controller.c, src/vt.c, systemd/tam-hided.service)
  passes host unit tests (make test) and end-to-end disposable KVM tests
  for startup auto-lock, VT_LOCKSWITCH, atomic handoff, socket peercred
  isolation, and SIGKILL + systemd Restart=always recovery (W5).

NEXT

  1. Define the compositor adapter interface (ext-session-lock-v1 lock
     confirmation, hotplug coverage, blanking/wake) and verify Hyprland's
     behavior in an isolated VM.
  2. Wire compositor adapter confirmation into tam-hided before handoff
     away from graphical sessions.
  3. Design and implement the privileged salted-hash passcode store, rate
     limiting, and multi-account/session picker.

WAITING FOR FRED

  Nothing.

WATCH OUT

  This project does not protect a workstation. No live login or seat
  changes without explicit approval and a recorded rollback point.
  Do not install systemd/tam-hided.service on a live host.
  Do not rely on vlock --all or VT_PROCESS (both failed open on SIGKILL).
  Graphical sessions must launch compositors via exec as session leader.
